    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a color-filtering assistant.\n\nThe input is ONE color record with these fields:\n\nName\nHEX\nRGB\n\nYour task is to determine whether this color is DARK.\n\nExtract the R, G, and B numbers from the RGB field.\n\nCalculate brightness using:\n\nbrightness = (0.299 × R) + (0.587 × G) + (0.114 × B)\n\nThe color is DARK only when:\n\nbrightness < 128\n\nIf the color is DARK, return exactly this JSON object:\n\n{\n\"name\": \"original Name\",\n\"Hex\": \"original HEX\",\n\"RGB\": \"rgb(R,G,B)\"\n}\n\nRules:\n\nPreserve the original Name exactly.\nPreserve the original HEX exactly.\nPreserve the RGB values exactly.\nRGB must always be a STRING.\nDo not change RGB into an array.\nDo not add any other properties.\nDo not add explanations.\nDo not use Markdown.\nReturn valid JSON only.\n\nIf the color is NOT DARK, return:\n\nnull\n\nInput color:\n\nName: {{ $json[\"﻿Name\"] }}\nHEX: {{ $json[\"HEX\"] }}\nRGB: {{ $json[\"RGB\"] }}",
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        448,
        0
      ],
      "id": "c355925e-0abe-4e34-a8ef-b7aaa3674d99",
